223
00:21:21,399 --> 00:21:26,760
February 22nd marks the birthday of Lord Robert Baden-Powell, the founder of the Scout Movement.

224
00:21:27,100 --> 00:21:34,000
And it is the World Organization of the Scout Movement's Founder's Day, an annual celebration.

225
00:21:34,179 --> 00:21:43,560
And nearly all national scout associations throughout the world celebrate Founder's Day as an opportunity to learn a little bit more about BP's life and his work.

226
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:51,040
In 1922, Baden-Powell spoke to the Third International Congress on Moral Education in Geneva, Switzerland.

227
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:58,580
His speech laid out a vision for Scouting as an education in peace and love in the aftermath of the ordeal of the First World War.

228
00:21:59,440 --> 00:22:04,879
And following the vision he laid out in that speech became the focus of the rest of Baden-Powell's life.

229
00:22:05,980 --> 00:22:11,040
You know, war's horrible devastation really influenced this old soldier.

230
00:22:11,040 --> 00:22:16,720
He was a very famous soldier and a hero to the British people.

231
00:22:18,159 --> 00:22:23,060
And he joined many others in looking for alternatives to armed conflict.

232
00:22:24,020 --> 00:22:32,120
And the speech suggests that Scouting could be used to foster world peace by giving young men and women an education and international goodwill.

233
00:22:32,120 --> 00:22:37,679
This really expansive and inspiring vision has yet to be fully realized.

234
00:22:38,560 --> 00:22:44,139
It's all too easy for us to lose sight of the international scope and possibilities of Scouting.

235
00:22:44,919 --> 00:22:49,020
You know, in our own personal involvement in the movement.

236
00:22:49,020 --> 00:22:56,680
Because we're focused on what we need to do that day and what's happening with our troop or our pack or our crew.

237
00:22:57,720 --> 00:23:04,100
But Founders Day represents an opportunity for us to focus on that aspect of Scouting, this world brotherhood.

238
00:23:04,660 --> 00:23:11,360
Let me read to you just one part of Baden-Powell's speech.

239
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:20,840
If such training be encouraged in all countries in such a manner that the rising generation throughout the world feel themselves tangibly linked in brotherhood,

240
00:23:21,240 --> 00:23:29,419
it is going to contribute markedly to the abolition of war and to that coming of the long-looked-for era of peace and goodwill among men.

